{# THE PAGE HINT — one row, at the bottom, and only where a page needs one.

   RULED: a page with something to explain says it ONCE, as a fragment, under
   the thing it is about. The files hub carried two cards of prose above its
   register and the design deleted them: a reader comes to a register to find
   something, and the explanation is what they want after they have failed to.
   So a hint sits at the BOTTOM, where the person still wondering will look,
   rather than above the content where everybody reads it on every visit
   forever.

   PARAMETERS:
     lead  the first few words, in bold — what the hint IS about, so a reader
           can tell in one glance whether it is theirs
     say   the rest of it, one sentence or two. Fragments, not an essay: what
           does not fit here belongs in the module's own docs
     icon  a ux-icons name, or nothing for the shell's own (`shell:info`)

   ONE PER PAGE. Two hints is an essay in instalments, and the second is the
   one nobody reads — which is why this is a partial a page includes once and
   not a list it feeds.

   THE MARKUP IS THE SHELL'S so every hint in the product reads alike, and a
   module that drew its own would be the fifth near-copy of the same card (the
   design had four, in four module sheets, under four names). The conformance
   suite refuses one. #}
<div class="pghint">
    {{ ux_icon(icon|default('shell:info')) }}
    <div><b>{{ lead }}</b> {{ say }}</div>
</div>
